<%# Admin site-wide usage dashboard (#221, ARCHITECTURE.md §8 — ADMIN-gated via
    Admin::BaseController). Renders ONLY the documented `@stats` (CalculationStats)
    methods — no queries here (that's backend turf). Built to docs/DESIGN.md (BLEND):
    a sweeping page title + green eyebrow, the volume in the shared `.stat-grid`, the
    30-day trend as a TradingView lightweight-charts Histogram (volume_trend_chart_controller,
    DESIGN.md §4 — every chart, dashboard charts included, uses the house JS library) over a
    no-JS data-table fallback, and thin-ruled BLEND data tables for the breakdowns + recent
    feed. Site-wide totals count ALL calculations incl. discarded (§6 — usage is usage); the
    recent feed flags discarded rows with a BLEND-styled badge and renders the raw echoed
    input → result values in a monospace <code> (DESIGN.md §2 — raw echoed data is <code>,
    not prose). %>
<% content_for :title, "Admin stats — whizwheel" %>

<% volume = @stats.volume %>
<% series = @stats.daily_series(days: 30) %>
<% attribution = @stats.attribution %>

<header>
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Admin · site-wide usage</p>
  <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Calculation statistics</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Every calculation run across whizwheel — all visitors, anonymous and signed-in.
    Totals count all usage, including history a user has soft-deleted from their own view.
  </p>
</header>

<%# ── Volume — the rolling-window counts as the shared stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat
    grid"). The all-time count is a plain unit-less number that can grow large, so the
    grid uses the sanctioned `--wide` track + `.stat-card--surface` (it sits on the cream
    page, not nested in a hero card). Tabular-nums + the never-clip net keep big counts
    whole. The "Today" card lifts its value to accent green (a positive/live figure, §1). %>
<section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="volume-heading">
  <h2 id="volume-heading" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Volume</h2>
  <dl class="mt-3 stat-grid stat-grid--wide">
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Today</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-accent break-words"><%= number_with_delimiter(volume[:today]) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Last 7 days</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words"><%= number_with_delimiter(volume[:last_7d]) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Last 30 days</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words"><%= number_with_delimiter(volume[:last_30d]) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card stat-card--surface">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">All time</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words"><%= number_with_delimiter(volume[:all_time]) %></dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<%# ── 30-day trend — a TradingView lightweight-charts Histogram series, drawn by
    volume_trend_chart_controller from the `series` JSON value (DESIGN.md §4 "Charts": every
    chart, dashboard charts included, uses the house JS library in its bar/histogram form —
    crosshair + per-bar tooltip). The underlying data is ALWAYS reachable without JS, so the
    same series is also rendered as a <details> data table; the controller hides it only
    after the chart paints, so the numbers never gate on JS (the only place hand-rolled
    markup is allowed now is this fallback). %>
<section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="trend-heading">
  <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]"
       data-controller="volume-trend-chart"
       data-volume-trend-chart-series-value="<%= series.map { |d| { date: d[:date].to_s, count: d[:count] } }.to_json %>">
    <h2 id="trend-heading" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Volume trend · last 30 days</h2>

    <%# Live lightweight-charts container — hidden until the controller draws into it (it
        injects its own <canvas>). Sized responsively (full width, fixed height). %>
    <div data-volume-trend-chart-target="chart" class="mt-4 h-60 w-full" hidden></div>

    <%# No-JS / accessible data fallback (DESIGN.md §4 "Charts"): the full series as a table.
        The controller retires this only once the chart paints. %>
    <div data-volume-trend-chart-target="fallback">
      <table class="mt-4 w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-rule text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-faint">
            <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold">Date</th>
            <th scope="col" class="py-2 text-right font-bold">Calculations</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% series.each do |day| %>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0">
              <td class="py-1.5 pr-4 text-muted"><%= day[:date].strftime("%b %-d") %></td>
              <td class="py-1.5 text-right tabular-nums text-ink"><%= number_with_delimiter(day[:count]) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Top calculators + Top users — two side-by-side BLEND data tables (thin rules,
    right-aligned tabular-nums counts). Stack on mobile, two columns on wider screens. %>
<section class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Top calculators</h2>
    <% top_calculators = @stats.top_calculators %>
    <% if top_calculators.any? %>
      <table class="mt-4 w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="sr-only">
          <tr><th scope="col">Calculator</th><th scope="col">Calculations</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% top_calculators.each do |row| %>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink"><%= row[:calculator] %></td>
              <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-muted"><%= number_with_delimiter(row[:count]) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">No calculations recorded yet.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Top users</h2>
    <% top_users = @stats.top_users %>
    <% if top_users.any? %>
      <table class="mt-4 w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="sr-only">
          <tr><th scope="col">User</th><th scope="col">Calculations</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% top_users.each do |row| %>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink"><%= row[:username] %></td>
              <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-muted"><%= number_with_delimiter(row[:count]) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">No signed-in usage recorded yet.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Anonymous vs. attributed split (DESIGN.md §4 data table). A simple two-row table
    with each side's share; site-wide and discarded-inclusive (§6). %>
<section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="attribution-heading">
  <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <h2 id="attribution-heading" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Anonymous vs. attributed</h2>
    <% attribution_total = attribution[:anonymous] + attribution[:attributed] %>
    <table class="mt-4 w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="sr-only">
        <tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Calculations</th><th scope="col">Share</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-rule">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink">Anonymous</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-right tabular-nums text-muted"><%= number_with_delimiter(attribution[:anonymous]) %></td>
          <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-faint"><%= attribution_total.zero? ? "—" : number_to_percentage(attribution[:anonymous] * 100.0 / attribution_total, precision: 1) %></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold text-ink">Attributed</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-right tabular-nums text-muted"><%= number_with_delimiter(attribution[:attributed]) %></td>
          <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-faint"><%= attribution_total.zero? ? "—" : number_to_percentage(attribution[:attributed] * 100.0 / attribution_total, precision: 1) %></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
      <tfoot>
        <tr class="border-t-2 border-ink">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold text-ink">Total</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-ink"><%= number_with_delimiter(attribution_total) %></td>
          <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-faint"></td>
        </tr>
      </tfoot>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Recent activity feed — the 50 most recent calculations (discarded included, §6),
    each tagged with a BLEND "Discarded" badge when soft-deleted (the `discarded` boolean).
    Anonymous rows (nil username) show "anonymous" in faint. Scrolls horizontally on
    narrow screens rather than overflowing (DESIGN.md §6). %>
<section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="recent-heading">
  <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <h2 id="recent-heading" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Recent activity</h2>
    <% recent = @stats.recent %>
    <% if recent.any? %>
      <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule text-left text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-faint">
              <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold">Calculator</th>
              <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold">Who</th>
              <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold">When</th>
              <th scope="col" class="py-2 font-bold">Summary</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% recent.each do |row| %>
              <tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0 align-top<%= " text-faint" if row[:discarded] %>">
                <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold <%= row[:discarded] ? "text-faint" : "text-ink" %>">
                  <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
                    <%= row[:calculator] %>
                    <% if row[:discarded] %>
                      <%# Discarded badge (DESIGN.md §4 — never colour alone): a coral-tinted
                          pill with explicit "Discarded" text, so a soft-deleted row reads
                          without relying on the row's muted colour. %>
                      <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-primary/30 bg-primary/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-primary">Discarded</span>
                    <% end %>
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 whitespace-nowrap">
                  <% if row[:username] %>
                    <span class="font-semibold <%= row[:discarded] ? "text-faint" : "text-ink" %>"><%= row[:username] %></span>
                  <% else %>
                    <span class="italic text-faint">anonymous</span>
                  <% end %>
                </td>
                <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums text-muted"><%= calculation_timestamp(row[:created_at]) %></td>
                <td class="py-2.5 text-muted">
                  <%# Raw echoed input → result values are quoted-back data, not a presented
                      answer — DESIGN.md §2 renders them in a monospace <code>, never plain prose. %>
                  <code class="font-mono text-sm <%= row[:discarded] ? "text-faint" : "text-muted" %>"><%= calculation_summary(row[:inputs], row[:result]) %></code>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">No calculations recorded yet.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
